  "question": {
    "text": "Select the nature or type of redox change in the following reaction:-<br />\r<br />\r<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Disproportionation",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Intramolecular redox",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Intermolecular redox",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of the above",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Auto-redox or disproportionation is the one in which same substance is oxidized and reduced as well.<br /><br />Intramolecular redox change is the one in which one element of a compound is oxidized and the other element is reduced.<br /><br />Intermolecular redox is the one in which one of the two reactants is oxidized and the other is reduced."
  }
}